---
import Sparkles from "lucide-astro/Sparkles";
import LayoutGrid from "lucide-astro/LayoutGrid";
import MousePointerClick from "lucide-astro/MousePointerClick";
import Shield from "lucide-astro/Shield";
import ExternalLink from "lucide-astro/ExternalLink";
import RefreshCw from "lucide-astro/RefreshCw";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/layout/PageHeader.astro";
import ResourceCard from "../components/ui/ResourceCard.astro";
import Accordion from "../components/ui/Accordion.astro";
import AccordionItem from "../components/ui/AccordionItem.astro";
import SuggestionForm from "../components/ui/SuggestionForm.astro";

const siteLastUpdated = "2026-03-15";
const siteLastUpdatedDisplay = "March 15, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Learn why this dashboard exists, what it does, and where the company data comes from."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="About"
    subtitle="Why this dashboard exists, what it does, and where the data comes from."
  />

  <section class="space-y-8">
    <!-- Overview (matches Hiring Tips section title + cards) -->
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-6">Overview</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <ResourceCard title="Why I built it" icon={Sparkles} tone="primary">
          <p>
            I kept coming back to the original list. It’s a great community
            resource, and I’m grateful it exists. I wanted a different way to
            browse it, and I wanted a project I could build and maintain.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-accent">
            <li>A calmer layout that’s easier to skim</li>
            <li>Quick links out to careers pages and details</li>
            <li>A small project I can keep improving</li>
          </ul>
        </ResourceCard>

        <ResourceCard
          title="What you can do here"
          icon={MousePointerClick}
          tone="secondary"
        >
          <p>
            Use this to find leads, then double check everything. It’s meant to
            save you a bit of time and mental overhead while you’re searching.
            Interview processes change, job posts go stale, and sometimes the
            notes are incomplete.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-accent">
            <li>Browse companies in a grid or list instead of a README</li>
            <li>See interview notes at a glance, when they exist</li>
            <li>Jump to the company site to verify what’s current</li>
          </ul>
        </ResourceCard>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Details (progressive disclosure) -->
    <Accordion
      title="Useful Information"
      description="Expand for notes on scope, design, and corrections."
    >
      <AccordionItem title="Website status" icon={RefreshCw}>
        <p
          class="ui-muted-body text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark"
        >
          Last updated: <time
            datetime={siteLastUpdated}
            class="font-medium text-text-light dark:text-text-dark"
            >{siteLastUpdatedDisplay}</time
          >
        </p>
        <ul
          class="ui-muted-body mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark marker:text-accent"
        >
          <li>
            Added curated resources on hiring research, AI in coding,
            accessibility, and tech-for-good job boards
          </li>
          <li>
            Companies can now request a verified badge through a simple
            verification form
          </li>
          <li>
            Interview process tags include AI-friendly categories like pair
            programming with AI tools
          </li>
          <li>
            Streamlined the resources page — fewer sections, better layout
          </li>
          <li>
            Broken careers URLs and outdated company notes fixed as they're
            found
          </li>
        </ul>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem title="What this isn’t" icon={Shield}>
        <p
          class="ui-muted-body text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark"
        >
          This site is not a stamp of approval. It’s a community-maintained
          list, shown in a different UI. Processes change.
        </p>
        <ul
          class="ui-muted-body mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark marker:text-accent"
        >
          <li>Not a hiring platform, and not a recruiter tool</li>
          <li>Not me vouching for a company</li>
          <li>Not a guarantee that an interview process stays the same</li>
        </ul>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem title="Design goals" icon={LayoutGrid}>
        <p
          class="ui-muted-body text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark"
        >
          I wanted to make the job hunt feel a little less draining. This UI
          helped me, so I’m sharing it in case it helps someone else too.
        </p>
        <ul
          class="ui-muted-body mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark marker:text-accent"
        >
          <li>Good contrast and focus styles, so it’s keyboard friendly</li>
          <li>Clear spacing and typography that’s easy on the eyes</li>
          <li>Less time fiddling with the UI, more time applying</li>
        </ul>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem title="Data source" icon={ExternalLink}>
        <p
          class="ui-muted-body text-sm text-text-mutedLight dark:text-text-mutedDark"
        >
          The company list comes from the upstream community repository. I sync
          updates from there when they’re published. Any local fixes or
          additions live in a separate local file, so the upstream data stays
          the source of truth.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/poteto/hiring-without-whiteboards"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-accent hover:underline focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
        >
          hiring-without-whiteboards
          <ExternalLink class="h-5 w-5" aria-hidden="true" />
        </a>
      </AccordionItem>
    </Accordion>

    <!-- Suggestion Form -->
    <div id="suggestions">
      <SuggestionForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
